{"paper_id": "paper-b014cdacd2234a55", "doi": "10.1159/000553584", "title": "From Zoonotic Spillover to Hemorrhagic Crisis: Molecular Insights and Epidemiology of Ethiopia’s 2025 Marburg Outbreak Amid Preparedness Gaps and Historical Lethality", "analysis": {"analysis": {"scope_and_question": "The review examines the molecular determinants of Marburg virus virulence, including GP-NPC1 mediated entry, VP24-driven interferon antagonism, and GP-associated endothelial dysfunction, alongside Ethiopia's 2025 outbreak in Jinka resulting from a zoonotic spillover.", "evidence_base_and_review_method": "The supplied evidence does not report the review type, databases, search dates, eligibility criteria, selection method, included-study count, or meta-analysis procedures.", "consensus_and_key_conclusions": "Ethiopia's first confirmed Marburg virus disease outbreak in Jinka involved nine laboratory-confirmed cases and eight deaths with a case fatality rate of 89% following a single spillover from Rousettus aegyptiacus amidst concurrent cholera and population displacement, while case confirmation was achieved within 48 hours, over 90% of contacts were traced, and L-gene sequencing placed the isolate within the East African lineage linked to the 2024 Rwanda outbreak.", "controversies_and_evidence_gaps": "The review highlights persistent constraints in diagnostics, clinical readiness, and countermeasure access in Ethiopia alongside the outbreak pressures of concurrent cholera and large-scale population displacement.", "research_and_practice_implications": "A feasible seven-day containment framework is outlined, integrating low-cost molecular testing, remdesivir therapy, and VSV-MARV ring vaccination to prevent further spread in resource-limited settings."}, "summary_en": "This review summarizes the molecular determinants of Marburg virus virulence and examines Ethiopia's initial Marburg virus disease outbreak in Jinka, which occurred via a spillover from Rousettus aegyptiacus during concurrent cholera and population displacement. The outbreak comprised nine confirmed cases and eight deaths, yielding an 89% case fatality rate. Despite these severe operational pressures, rapid case confirmation was achieved within 48 hours, more than 90% of contacts were traced, and same-day L-gene sequencing identified the isolate as belonging to the East African lineage associated with the 2024 Rwanda outbreak. The paper also contrasts these genomic and coordination strengths with persistent constraints in diagnostics, clinical readiness, and countermeasure access. To address these challenges, a feasible seven-day containment framework integrating low-cost molecular testing, remdesivir therapy, and VSV-MARV ring vaccination is proposed for resource-limited settings.", "evidence_ids": {"scope_and_question": ["A1", "A4"], "evidence_base_and_review_method": ["A2"], "consensus_and_key_conclusions": ["A1", "A3"], "controversies_and_evidence_gaps": ["A2", "A4"], "research_and_practice_implications": ["A5"]}, "confidence": "low", "postprocess_audit": {"removed_duplicate_sentences": 0, "repaired_incomplete_fields": [], "evidence_replacements": [], "policy": "v10-exclusive-rhetorical-fields-1"}, "language_contract": {"policy_version": "v17.1-source-language-safe-english-1", "source_language": "en", "verified_english": true, "replacements": [], "original_evidence_preserved": false}, "status": "passed", "kind": "review", "provider": "gemini", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "attempts": [{"task": "paper_review_analysis", "provider": "gemini", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "retry_index": 0, "at": "2026-07-22T13:49:22+00:00", "system_chars": 4668, "prompt_chars": 6687, "status": "success", "response_model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "elapsed_ms": 2257, "parser_audit": {"policy_version": "v17.2-flexible-json-parser-1", "method": "direct_json", "response_chars": 2925, "repaired": false, "truncated_signal": false}, "normalization_audit": {"policy_version": "v17.2-preval